    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Across the whole packet, policy debate follows one dominant pattern shown by the cited source.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f96264d3ee66a01f\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, in Syria will the Government seek to use the Euphrates river as a boundary between Assad’s forces and the YPG and others? I suggest that such a separation of forces would save lives and prevent unnecessary clashes. Does the noble Earl agree that some minimal level of British representation in Damascus would facilitate the separation of forces and any transition in Syria?I\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_d55816a7ba53dafb\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, the Minister has been meticulous in not thanking or supporting the inspector for her report. I invite him to do so. During my 12 years in government I came across Dame Glenys Stacey, and she is one of the finest public servants I had contact with during my time as a Minister. She deserves incredible support and the thanks of the House for the report, and I should like to\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_5654908e530b48dc\",\"quote\":\"I welcome what the Secretary of State has said about his efforts to secure further Hawk orders. May I remind him that if we do not get those Hawk orders for BAE Systems and the jobs at Brough, his Department will not be able to renew the Red Arrows fleet, which flies Hawks, when the time comes?\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_5dbce1ef175b9a97\",\"quote\":\"The accounts show that in the last four years, on the PFI contracts alone, Carillion was part of deals that have made nearly £1 billion in profit directly from the public purse It is now clear that the notion, which all Governments have dealt with, that PFI is a good way to transfer risk to the private sector is a myth. Will the Government finally bring in a windfall tax to claw\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f96264d3ee66a01f\",\"quote\":\"My Lords, in Syria will the Government seek to use the Euphrates river as a boundary between Assad’s forces and the YPG and others? I suggest that such a separation of forces would save lives and prevent unnecessary clashes. Does the noble Earl agree that some minimal level of British representation in Damascus would facilitate the separation of forces and any transition in Syria?I\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"The cited sources discuss specific policy debates (Syria, Hawk orders, PFI) without establishing a single, dominant pattern across all of them.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely asserts a unified policy debate, ignoring the diverse and specific contexts of the discussions.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The excerpts represent distinct policy discussions with no overarching pattern.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim makes a broad generalization about a 'dominant pattern' across all cited sources, which is not supported by the individual excerpts. Each excerpt focuses on a different policy issue and debate, rendering a single, overarching pattern impossible to establish. The evidence demonstrates a lack of warrant for this claim.\"}",
